        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: కర్తవ్యం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కర్తవ్యం — kartavyaṁ — \"a duty; an obligation\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "తల్లిదండ్రులను చూసుకోవడం మన కర్తవ్యం. tallidaṇḍrulanu cūsukōvaḍaṁ mana kartavyaṁ. Looking after our parents is our duty."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A higher word than బాధ్యత: a moral duty."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కర్తవ్యం (kartavyaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit kartavya, \"to be done\", and as a noun \"that which ought to be done, a duty\" (Monier-Williams), from kṛ, \"to do\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
